# kod-infra-dsh on abc-prod-02 (colocated with auth.kodeme.io). Copy to
# .env.kod-infra-dsh (gitignored). Store real values only in the local ignored
# file and Dokploy, never in Git.
#
# Authentication is Authentik forward-auth at the Traefik layer, not a gateway
# password, so there are no DSH_BASIC_* values. AUTHENTIK_HOST is not a secret
# and is set in the instance manifest's env_overrides.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=kod-infra-dsh
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Required. Long random value shared with the Traefik middleware chain that
# proves a request passed the Authentik gate. Generate once with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
GATEWAY_AUTH_SECRET=
# FRIDAY runner (the `friday` service in kodemeio-dsh's docker-compose.prod.yml).
# FRIDAY_RUNNER_TOKEN is the bearer the friday_dispatch worker presents to
# POST /run (openssl rand -hex 32); FRIDAY_LLM_API_KEY is FRIDAY's own LiteLLM
# virtual key ("friday", with its own daily budget). Both are deliberately
# NON-FATAL at render time (final review I7): this declarative path never
# carried them, and a FRIDAY-only value must not make the web Harness
# un-renderable. friday-server.mjs refuses to start without them, so a
# declarative apply that omits them runs the rest of the stack and leaves
# `friday` exiting 1 -- FRIDAY down, nothing else affected. Set the real values
# here only when the declarative path should run FRIDAY too, and keep them in
# sync with Dokploy's env store (rollout runbook Step 3/5).
FRIDAY_RUNNER_TOKEN=
FRIDAY_LLM_API_KEY=
